, abstract =    "This paper presents a general framework for the design
and randomized analysis of geometric algorithms.  These algorithms are
on-line and the framework provides general bounds for their expected space
and time complexities when averaging over all permutations of the input
data.  The method is general and can be applied to various geometric
problems.  The power of the technique is illustrated by new efficient
on-line algorithms for constructing convex hulls and Voronoi diagrams in
any dimension, Voronoi diagrams of line segments in the plane,
arrangements of curves in the plane and others."
}

