                 a partition of the points into k subsets (clusters). For any
                 fixed k, we can find a k-clustering which minimizes any monotone
                 function of the diameters or the radii of the
                 clusters in polynomial time. The algorithm is based on the
                 fact that any two clusters in an optimal solution can
                 be separated by a line."
}

