, annote =      "Uses 3D DT by insertion."
, abstract =    "A finite element package for the computation of
                 three-dimensional magnetostatic field is described. The
                 finite element mesh is automatically built in two steps
                 using a Delaunay tetrahedrization. In step 1, the user
                 gives interactively a first set of nodes located on
                 interfaces and boundaries, and the program computes a
                 coarse tetrahedral mesh. In step 2, the program adds
                 new nodes automatically to refine the initial mesh and
                 regularizes it. The implemented finite element
                 formulations use either scalar or vector potential. The
                 postprocessor allows interactive computation and
                 visualization of any local or global quantities given
                 by closed formulas. 9 refs."
