, volume =      31
, number =      4
, year =        1989
, pages =       "191--196"
, annote =      "CDT is used to compute GT. DT is constrained to
                 include all the edges of the GT so far. Next edge can
                 be found in time O(n)."
, abstract =    "We show that the greedy triangulation of n points in
                 the plane can be computed in O(n**2 log n) time and
                 O(n) memory and storage. In particular we show that, by
                 maintaining a generalized Delaunay triangulation, the
                 next edge to be added to the greedy triangulation can
                 be found in O(n) time. Furthermore, if the generalized
                 Delaunay triangulation of a simple polygon could be
                 computed in O(n) time, our algorithm would compute the
                 greedy triangulation in O(n**2) time. (Author abstract)
                 13 Refs."
}

