                 distance-doubling strategy. This algorithm is designed
                 for implementation on a fine-grain parallel computer
                 such as the connection machine. It is shown how the
                 algorithm is extended to calculation of
                 distance-from-region computations and the use of
                 nonstandard metrics. Two algorithms are presented for
                 the calculation of the Voronoi diagram over one- and
                 two- dimensional lattices. Both algorithms propagate
                 the explicit location of the nearest Voronoi point
                 rather than the distance to the point and so are more
                 accurate than traditional methods. The first algorithm
                 is based on brushfire propagation while the second
                 algorithm relies on distance doubling. It is found that
                 the distance-doubling algorithm is more efficient than
                 the classical algorithm when at least one Voronoi
                 polygon is large. It is found that there is little
                 penalty in using the updated brushfire algorithm over
                 the traditional algorithm. 6 Refs."
}

