                 an upper bound 2n minus 6 to d(T//1,T//2), using
                 triangulation of polyhedra. Makinen has subsequently
                 shown that a weaker upper bound of 2n minus 5 can be
                 simply proved with elementary tree concepts. In this
                 note we present a new tree transformation algorithm,
