, keywords =    "Delaunay partitioning, semiconductor models, scharfetter-gummel discretization, Voronoi cross-sections"
, annote =      "Incremental algorithm in 3D. First take a surrounding
                 tetra. Connect new point to all points of tetra whose
                 c-sphere it lies in. Delete edges that are only in bad
                 tetrahedra. Yet another proof."
, abstract =    "An algorithm for Delaunay partitioning in three
                 dimensions is given, and its use in numerical
                 semiconductor models is examined. In particular,
                 tetrahedral elements are found to be compatible with
                 the Scharfetter-Gummel discretization of the stationary
                 continuity equations associated with such models, using
                 the Voronoi cross-sections for each edge in the
                 obtained network. For tetrahedral elements, however,
                 the Voronoi cross-sections do not coincide with those
                 previously shown to be compatible with the
                 Scharfetter-Gummel method. (Author abstract) 16 refs."
}

