@inproceedings{zik-eprtn-98
, author =      "Sergey Zhukov and Andrei Iones and G. Kronin"
, title =       "Environment Preprocessing for Real-Time Navigation of Intelligent Agents"
, booktitle =   "Proc. SCCG'98 Conference in Bratislava ??"
, month =       apr
, year =        1998
, comments =    "
This is Andrei Iones and Sergey Zhukov from St-Petersburg State Technical
University, Russia.
\par
We are studying the problem of intelligent agent navigation in complex
environments. The goal of our research is to develop a technique
(and theoretical foundations) to solve the navigation problem.
We assume that our algorithms must be applicable to the agents
with significantly different locomotion capabilities that live
(navigate) in {\em really} complex 3D environments, including
natural landscapes with caves, stalactites/stalagmites, etc.
Our characters (agents) are spiders, birds, hoppers, etc., so
they have totally different 'walk algorithms'. Since we have
to handle all these creature types motivated us to develop
such 'universal' techniques that:
- enables the agent to explore the environment off-line (it takes
  5 to 30 minutes) and create a representative map;
- navigate in the environment in real-time using the map.
\par
The technology is not heuristic - it can be proved that
the paths found in real-time do not differ much from the
real optimal paths.
Currently, our technology is practically implemented in a
commercial 3D title scheduled this year.
\par
We base our technology on accessibility graphs, not on
road maps/visibility graphs since these methods prove to be
inefficient in our context."
, update =      "98.07 mitchell"
}

